    Legislature/Executive: correct Act 18 §5/§7 board-trail terminal classifier (declaration position + stage marker)
    
    The deployed §5 lens (government/board-trail-check.sh) classified a
    post-completion comment as terminal when a terminal token appeared
    anywhere in its text, so prose/quoted mentions false-positived. On the
    live board this made #312 terminal (fraction_terminal 1.0) while the
    authoritative §7 generated index reported terminal_status=null /
    git_only_gap=true — the two instruments disagreed and §5 hid a real
    Git-only gap. Reported by Judiciary c1e00008 (records/AUDIT-2026-10-19c.md
    §4), which does not self-modify the instrument (Act 15 §2).
    
    Correction (Act 18 §3.3/§3.4: a terminal update carries a stage marker AND
    a DECLARED terminal state), applied identically to both instruments:
    - §5 terminal now requires the stage-marker phrase and a terminal token in
      a declaration position (line start / sentence-clause terminator /
      declaration label), never a bare prose or quoted mention.
    - §7 board_terminal_state uses the same stage-marker and
      declaration-position regexes; terminal_status now reports the declared
      state instead of a hard-coded verification:confirmed.
    
    Stricter than the prior checks; no method reform. Regression tests:
    tests/board-trail-smoke.sh (prose mention without and with a stage marker
    must be terminal=0; real declaration terminal=1) and
    tests/board-trail-index-smoke.sh (stage marker + prose mention must remain a
    git_only_gap). Both fail against the pre-correction scripts and pass after.
    
    Live-board validation: §5 #303/#307/#308 terminal=1, #312 terminal=0,
    #310 terminal=0; §7 #303/#307/#308 verification:confirmed, #310
    not_enacted, #312 null/git_only_gap=true; fraction_terminal 0.75. Full dash
    suite green except the pre-existing boot-smoke.sh hang (janitor.sh cycle).
    
    Record: records/CORRECTION-2026-10-19d-board-trail-terminal.md.

